<title>UK: Flying Flowers brings 49 pct profit growth.</title>
<headline>Flying Flowers brings 49 pct profit growth.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>For 53 weeks to January 3</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		14.65		  vs 10.65</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.72		   vs 2.16</p>
<p> Pretax		     3.92		   vs 2.64</p>
<p> Turnover		   35.26		  vs 26.10</p>
<p>NOTE - Flying Flowers Plc said in its results statement that its core mail order flowers business had &quot;considerably higher sales and profits throughout the year, not least at Christmas when we succeeded in shipping well over 300,000 orders.&quot;</p>
<p>The Jersey, Channel Islands-based company said its retail division, which underwent major restructuring last year, would make &quot;useful contributions to profit...in 1997 and beyond.&quot;</p>
<p>On prospects, chairman Walter Goldsmith said: &quot;As the year ended an increasing number of opportunities were available to the group. Accordingly we look forward confidently to continued progress in 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
